    "text": "To determine how much Henry gets paid to sell and paint 8 bikes, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Determine how much Henry is paid to sell one bike.\n2. Calculate the total payment for selling and painting 8 bikes.\n\nFirst, we know that Henry gets $5 to paint one bike. According to the problem, he is paid $8 more to sell one bike than he is paid to paint it. Therefore, the payment for selling one bike is:\n\\[ 5 + 8 = 13 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nNext, we need to find out how much Henry gets paid for selling and painting 8 bikes. Since he gets $13 for selling one bike and $5 for painting one bike, the total payment for one bike (both selling and painting) is:\n\\[ 13 + 5 = 18 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nNow, we calculate the total payment for 8 bikes:\n\\[ 18 \\times 8 = 144 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nThus, the total amount Henry gets paid to sell and paint 8 bikes is:\n\\[ \\boxed{144} \\]",
